OL,3,AHouthi rebel advance in Yemen may
OL,4,Afurther destabilise global economy
OL,5,
OL,6,FYemen, a mountainous, heavily armed,
OL,7,Fintensely tribal and largely
OL,8,Fimpoverished nation, sits at the far
OL,9,Fsouth-west corner of the Arabian
OL,10,FPeninsula.
OL,12,FThe country has two coasts: One faces
OL,13,Fthe Indian Ocean on which sits the
OL,14,Fonce-prosperous trading port of Aden,
OL,15,Fthe other faces the Red Sea and, most
OL,16,Fimportantly, the narrow chokepoint at
OL,17,Fthe southern exit of that waterway -
OL,18,Fthe so-called Bab al-Mandab Strait or,
OL,19,Fin English, The Gate of Tears.
OL,23,APub: 16-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
